-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/6y3zli1mpb66xt6/9419a52f-9f24-4a96-96b7-2e6750c7102c/a6f650a0-52b3-11f1-a9b9-434ea329edcd/file-6y3zli1mpb66xt7.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/6y3zli1mpb66xt6/9419a52f-9f24-4a96-96b7-2e6750c7102c/a6f650a0-52b3-11f1-a9b9-434ea329edcd/file-6y3zli1mpb66xt7.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/6y3zli1mpb66xt6/9419a52f-9f24-4a96-96b7-2e6750c7102c/a6f650a0-52b3-11f1-a9b9-434ea329edcd/file-6y3zli1mpb66xt7.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/6y3zli1mpb66xt6/9419a52f-9f24-4a96-96b7-2e6750c7102c/a6f650a0-52b3-11f1-a9b9-434ea329edcd/file-6y3zli1mpb66xt7.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p><img alt=\"JEE Advanced 2026 Paper 1 Online Chemistry - Aldehydes, Ketones and Carboxylic Acids Question 6 English Explanation 2\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/6y3zli1mpb677rg/94ef643b-41f3-4f69-87ab-320c47926840/aea664c0-52b3-11f1-a9b9-434ea329edcd/file-6y3zli1mpb677rh.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/6y3zli1mpb677rg/94ef643b-41f3-4f69-87ab-320c47926840/aea664c0-52b3-11f1-a9b9-434ea329edcd/file-6y3zli1mpb677rh.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;max-height:40vh;vertical-align:baseline\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/6y3zli1mpb677rg/94ef643b-41f3-4f69-87ab-320c47926840/aea664c0-52b3-11f1-a9b9-434ea329edcd/file-6y3zli1mpb677rh.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/6y3zli1mpb677rg/94ef643b-41f3-4f69-87ab-320c47926840/aea664c0-52b3-11f1-a9b9-434ea329edcd/file-6y3zli1mpb677rh.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/6y3zli1mpb677rg/94ef643b-41f3-4f69-87ab-320c47926840/aea664c0-52b3-11f1-a9b9-434ea329edcd/file-6y3zli1mpb677rh.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/6y3zli1mpb677rg/94ef643b-41f3-4f69-87ab-320c47926840/aea664c0-52b3-11f1-a9b9-434ea329edcd/file-6y3zli1mpb677rh.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/6y3zli1mpb677rg/94ef643b-41f3-4f69-87ab-320c47926840/aea664c0-52b3-11f1-a9b9-434ea329edcd/file-6y3zli1mpb677rh.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/6y3zli1mpb677rg/94ef643b-41f3-4f69-87ab-320c47926840/aea664c0-52b3-11f1-a9b9-434ea329edcd/file-6y3zli1mpb677rh.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p><b>Understanding the role of LiBH<sub>4</sub></b></p>\n<p>LiBH<sub>4</sub> is a reducing agent. It converts <b>esters</b> into <b>alcohols</b>, but it does not reduce the <b>carboxylic acid group</b>. This selectivity helps in predicting which groups will change during the reaction and which will remain the same.</p>\n<p><b>Forming the products</b></p>\n<p>In the reaction, only the ester group gets reduced. The carboxylic acid group stays unchanged. Based on this, different compounds form as products, which are labelled as <b>P, Q, R,</b> and <b>S</b>.</p>\n<p><b>Relationship between products</b></p>\n<p>The pairs <b>P and Q</b> have the same connectivity but differ in the spatial arrangement of atoms. Similarly, <b>R and S</b> also differ in spatial arrangement. These are examples of <b>diastereomers</b>, which are a type of stereoisomer that are not mirror images of each other.</p>\n<p><b>Type of isomerism</b></p>\n<p>Since the difference arises due to the geometry around the double bond or restricted rotation, <b>P and Q</b> as well as <b>R and S</b> are specifically <b>geometrical isomers</b>, which are a form of diastereomers.</p>\n<p>Therefore, <b>P and Q are diastereomers</b> and <b>R and S are diastereomers</b> because they are <b>geometrical isomers</b>.</p>"}},"subject":"chemistry","timeAllotted":180000,"topic":"preparation-properties-and-uses-of-carboxylic-acids","type":"mcq","year":2026,"yearKey":"jee-advanced-2026-paper-1-online","active":true,"options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"<p><b>P & Q</b> are identical, and <b>R & S</b> are diastereomers.</p>"},{"identifier":"B","content":"<p><b>P & Q</b> are diastereomers, and <b>R & S</b> are identical.</p>"},{"identifier":"C","content":"<p><b>P & Q</b> are diastereomers, and <b>R & S</b> are diastereomers.</p>"},{"identifier":"D","content":"<p><b>P & Q</b> are identical, and <b>R & S</b> are identical.</p>"}],"correct_options":["C"],"explanation":"<p><img alt=\"JEE Advanced 2026 Paper 1 Online Chemistry - Aldehydes, Ketones and Carboxylic Acids Question 6 English Explanation 1\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/6y3zli1mpb66xt6/9419a52f-9f24-4a96-96b7-2e6750c7102c/a6f650a0-52b3-11f1-a9b9-434ea329edcd/file-6y3zli1mpb66xt7.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/6y3zli1mpb66xt6/9419a52f-9f24-4a96-96b7-2e6750c7102c/a6f650a0-52b3-11f1-a9b9-434ea329edcd/file-6y3zli1mpb66xt7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;max-height:40vh;vertical-align:baseline\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/6y3zli1mpb66xt6/9419a52f-9f24-4a96-96b7-2e6750c7102c/a6f650a0-52b3-11f1-a9b9-434ea329edcd/file-6y3zli1mpb66xt7.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/6y3zli1mpb66xt6/9419a52f-9f24-4a96-96b7-2e6750c7102c/a6f650a0-52b3-11f1-a9b9-434ea329edcd/file-6y3zli1mpb66xt7.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/6y3zli1mpb66xt6/9419a52f-9f24-4a96-96b7-2e6750c7102c/a6f650a0-52b3-11f1-a9b9-434ea329edcd/file-6y3zli1mpb66xt7.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/6y3zli1mpb66xt6/9419a52f-9f24-4a96-96b7-2e6750c7102c/a6f650a0-52b3-11f1-a9b9-434ea329edcd/file-6y3zli1mpb66xt7.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/6y3zli1mpb66xt6/9419a52f-9f24-4a96-96b7-2e6750c710